<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<TcPlcObject Version="1.1.0.1">
  <DUT Name="ST_CoEIndSub" Id="{62fd4c96-1a38-4aeb-82f8-1dcf9193e68a}">
    <Declaration><![CDATA[TYPE ST_CoEIndSub :

(*
    Purpose: CoE (CANopen over EtherCAT) object dictionary address of one
    VAT590 needle-valve controller parameter, carried as the index/subindex pair
    that the CoE read and write services address.

    Usage: FB_VCN_VAT590 (POUs/Functions/Valves/FB_VCN_VAT590.TcPOU) holds one
    ST_CoEIndSub constant per controller parameter it exchanges - cPressCtrl
    16#2199, the adaptive-downstream and fixed controller parameters 16#219A to
    16#21B3, the soft-pump parameters 16#21B9 to 16#21BC and the two position
    limits 16#56B3 / 16#56B4 - and copies their nIndex / nSubIndex into fbCoeRead
    (FB_CoERead_ByDriveRef) and fbCoeWrite (FB_CoEWrite_ByDriveRef) of
    Tc2_EtherCAT on every exchange. FB_CoE_FastRead in LCLSGeneral passes the same
    pair on to FB_CoERead_ByDriveRef, the index being the 8010 in 8010:12 and the
    subindex the 12.

    Objectives: state that the pair is a raw object dictionary address and not a
    physical quantity, so that a further parameter is added by looking up its
    index in the VAT590 CoE documentation instead of copying a literal, and so
    that these values are never scaled or compared against a limit.

    History:
      2022-04-10  Janez Govednik <janezg@slac.stanford.edu>: created with the CoE
                  interface of FB_VCN_VAT590 (commit 8d44a64), without a header
                  and without a comment on either member.
      2026-11-28  Header and member comments added; no member, type, order or
                  default value changed (audit finding #584, convention
                  conv_321640e095c0, task #458).
*)

STRUCT
    nIndex : WORD;    // CoE object dictionary index, hexadecimal (e.g. 16#2199); raw address, unitless
    nSubIndex : BYTE; // CoE object dictionary subindex within nIndex, 0 = whole object; raw address, unitless
END_STRUCT
END_TYPE
]]></Declaration>
  </DUT>
</TcPlcObject>